WEBVTT

00:00.430 --> 00:01.545
- [Voiceover] We're asked to find the sum

00:01.545 --> 00:05.167
of the first 50 terms of this series,

00:05.167 --> 00:06.537
and you might immediately recognize

00:06.537 --> 00:08.118
it is a geometric series.

00:08.118 --> 00:11.098
When we go from one term to
the next, what are we doing?

00:11.098 --> 00:15.108
Well, we're multiplying by
10/11, to go from one to 10/11,

00:15.108 --> 00:17.798
you multiply by 10 over 11,

00:17.798 --> 00:20.965
then you multiply by 10 over 11 again,

00:23.235 --> 00:24.265
and we keep doing this,

00:24.265 --> 00:26.908
and we wanna find the
first 50 terms of it.

00:26.908 --> 00:29.731
So we can apply the formula we derived

00:29.731 --> 00:33.289
for the sum of a finite geometric series

00:33.289 --> 00:35.540
and that tells us that the sum of,

00:35.540 --> 00:37.951
let's say in this case the first 50 terms,

00:37.951 --> 00:40.023
actually let me do it down here,

00:40.023 --> 00:42.690
so the sum of the first 50 terms

00:45.955 --> 00:50.623
is going to be equal to the
first term, which is one,

00:50.623 --> 00:53.706
so it's gonna be one times one minus,

00:55.049 --> 00:56.820
let me do that in a different color,

00:56.820 --> 00:59.903
one times one minus the common ratio,

01:01.621 --> 01:05.788
so the common ratio here is
10/11, 10/11 to the 50th power,

01:07.943 --> 01:10.902
to the power of how many terms we have,

01:10.902 --> 01:15.358
all of that over one
minus our common ratio.

01:15.358 --> 01:18.405
And so I'm not gonna solve it completely,

01:18.405 --> 01:20.214
but we can simplify this a little bit,

01:20.214 --> 01:22.286
this is gonna be one minus,

01:22.286 --> 01:24.178
let me put parenthesis
here just to make sure

01:24.178 --> 01:26.570
we're not just taking
10 to the 50th power.

01:26.570 --> 01:30.737
So one minus 10/11 to the 50th power over,

01:32.863 --> 01:37.292
this is 11/11 minus 10/11 is one over 11,

01:37.292 --> 01:38.251
and so this is the same thing

01:38.251 --> 01:40.470
as multiplying the numerator by 11,

01:40.470 --> 01:43.137
and so this is gonna be equal to

01:44.078 --> 01:48.245
11 times one minus 10/11 to the 50thpower,

01:50.008 --> 01:52.475
and you can try to
simplify this even more,

01:52.475 --> 01:53.337
but this gets up pretty far,

01:53.337 --> 01:55.717
at this point it is just arithmetic.

01:55.717 --> 01:58.516
Let's do another one of
these, this is kinda fun.

01:58.516 --> 02:02.099
So this is more clearly
a geometric series,

02:03.005 --> 02:05.199
and let's just first
think about how many terms

02:05.199 --> 02:06.180
we're gonna take the sum of.

02:06.180 --> 02:07.013
You might be tempted to say

02:07.013 --> 02:09.176
"Okay I'm gonna take it to the 79th power,

02:09.176 --> 02:12.087
"there must be 79 terms
here", but be very careful,

02:12.087 --> 02:13.983
because the first term is
when we're taking things

02:13.983 --> 02:17.619
to the zeroth power, we're
taking 0.99 to the zeroth power.

02:17.619 --> 02:21.146
The second term is where we're
taking it to the first power,

02:21.146 --> 02:23.325
the third term is where we're
taking it to the second power,

02:23.325 --> 02:27.271
the fourth term is where we're
taking it to the third power

02:27.271 --> 02:31.963
so on and so forth, so this
right over here is the 80th,

02:31.963 --> 02:34.046
the 80th term, 80th term.

02:35.795 --> 02:39.962
So we wanna find S sub 80, and
so this is gonna be equal to

02:41.393 --> 02:44.393
our first term is gonna be one times

02:47.384 --> 02:51.134
one minus our common
ratio to the 80th power,

02:52.687 --> 02:56.266
to the 80th power, all over,
and I'm leaving a blank

02:56.266 --> 02:58.278
because we still need to
figure out our common ratio,

02:58.278 --> 03:00.845
all over one minus our common ratio.

03:00.845 --> 03:02.102
So at first you might say

03:02.102 --> 03:05.071
well maybe the common ratio here is 0.99,

03:05.071 --> 03:08.320
but notice we have a change in sign here,

03:08.320 --> 03:10.722
and the key thing is to say
well to go from term to the next

03:10.722 --> 03:12.383
what are we multiplying by?

03:12.383 --> 03:15.982
Well to go from the first
term to the second term,

03:15.982 --> 03:18.399
we multiply by negative 0.99.

03:19.604 --> 03:24.420
And then, so we're
multiplying by negative 0.99.

03:24.420 --> 03:25.863
Now to go to the next term,

03:25.863 --> 03:29.280
we're again multiplying by negative 0.99,

03:30.665 --> 03:34.082
so the common ratio is not positive 0.99,

03:36.244 --> 03:38.994
but negative zero, negative 0.99,

03:39.960 --> 03:42.960
so let me write that, negative 0.99,

03:45.734 --> 03:49.524
and of course that is going
to be to the 80th power,

03:49.524 --> 03:52.274
all over one minus negative 0.99.

03:56.046 --> 03:59.126
And so we could simplify
this a little bit,

03:59.126 --> 04:01.886
this is all going to be equal to,

04:01.886 --> 04:04.449
oh that one we don't have to
worry too much about that,

04:04.449 --> 04:07.279
and so this is going to be one minus,

04:07.279 --> 04:10.890
so negative 0.99 to the 80th power,

04:10.890 --> 04:12.376
I should put parenthesis
there to make sure

04:12.376 --> 04:16.543
we are taking the negative
0.99 to the 80th power.

04:17.417 --> 04:19.429
Well, we're taking it to an even power,

04:19.429 --> 04:21.217
so it's going to be positive,
so that's going to be

04:21.217 --> 04:24.634
the same thing as 0.99 to the 80th power,

04:26.978 --> 04:30.679
and all of that over, well
subtracting a negative

04:30.679 --> 04:33.181
that's just gonna be adding the positive,

04:33.181 --> 04:35.264
so all of that over 1.99,

04:36.870 --> 04:39.471
and we could attempt to
simplify it more but,

04:39.471 --> 04:41.009
if we had a calculator we could

04:41.009 --> 04:44.327
actually find this exact
value or close value actually,

04:44.327 --> 04:47.032
most calculators don't
give you the exact value

04:47.032 --> 04:49.153
when you take something to the 80th power,

04:49.153 --> 04:52.715
but this is what that sum is going to be.

04:52.715 --> 04:54.984
Let's do one more of these.

04:54.984 --> 04:58.511
Alright, so here we have a
series defined recursively

04:58.511 --> 05:01.056
and so it's useful to just think about

05:01.056 --> 05:02.435
what it would actually look like.

05:02.435 --> 05:06.435
So the first term is 10,
and then the next term,

05:07.575 --> 05:11.076
so the second term A sub two is equal to

05:11.076 --> 05:14.231
A sub one times 9/10, alright.

05:14.231 --> 05:16.890
So the next term is gonna be
the previous term times 9/10,

05:16.890 --> 05:19.919
so it's gonna be 10 times nine over 10,

05:19.919 --> 05:22.018
and then the next term
is gonna be that times,

05:22.018 --> 05:23.237
is gonna be the second term,

05:23.237 --> 05:25.879
the third term is the
second term times 9/10,

05:25.879 --> 05:30.618
so 10 times nine over
10, nine over 10 squared.

05:30.618 --> 05:32.417
And the way it's written right now,

05:32.417 --> 05:36.838
we don't have it written as
a finite geometric series,

05:36.838 --> 05:38.549
so let's say we wanna take the sum,

05:38.549 --> 05:41.466
let's say we want the sum of first,

05:43.698 --> 05:46.031
first I don't know 30 terms,

05:46.882 --> 05:48.715
sum of first 30 terms.

05:49.892 --> 05:51.320
So what will this be?

05:51.320 --> 05:55.487
Well we're gonna take S sub
one, S sub 30, oh I wrote ten,

05:57.778 --> 06:00.042
S sub 30, the sum of the first 30 terms,

06:00.042 --> 06:03.436
is gonna be equal to the first
term, we've done this before,

06:03.436 --> 06:07.436
the first term times one
minus the common ratio,

06:08.503 --> 06:12.253
one minus the common
ratio to the 30th power,

06:13.795 --> 06:17.462
all of that over one
minus the common ratio.

06:18.511 --> 06:20.853
And let's see we could, one minus 9/10,

06:20.853 --> 06:24.026
this is 1/10 right over
here, you divide by 1/10,

06:24.026 --> 06:25.991
this is the same thing
as multiplying by 100,

06:25.991 --> 06:30.158
so this is gonna be 100
times one minus 9/10 to the,

06:32.769 --> 06:36.936
oh let me write it this
way, 9/10 to the 30th power.

06:37.819 --> 06:40.402
And, actually these
parenthesis you always wanna

06:40.402 --> 06:41.960
put parenthesis there to make sure we see

06:41.960 --> 06:43.991
we're taking both the nine and the 10

06:43.991 --> 06:46.143
or the 9/10, the whole
thing to the 30th power,

06:46.143 --> 06:49.726
not just the nine, so
there you go, did I..

06:51.732 --> 06:53.869
yep there you go we're done.
